      "message": "1) I\u0027m not sure what to make of the comment. When I read \"execute independently\", I think that without detach(), the child thread is blocked on some action from the parent thread.\n\nBut I thought all detach() really meant was \"we\u0027re not going to join this thread, so discard any state we\u0027d need to join\".\n\nAnd if that understanding is correct, then I think the comment is unnecessary.\n\n2) If we\u0027re detach()-ing the thread, does the thread still need to be a member variable? Seems like an opportunity for bugs. (We might try to join() the thread, and thereby generate an exception.)",
